<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-code-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hannezo, Prost & Joanny (2014) PNAS & Krajnc & Ziherl (2015) PRE 3D epithelial sheet morphology (squamous-to-cuboidal-to-columnar scaling, apico-basal buckling & Gómez-Gálvez scutoid tube packing) — Code-to-model traceability: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module header maps Laws 1-5 to the Lean theorem names and to the cited equations, and the Pass 3 section states plainly what the mesh is and is not (L30-57, L59-100); function docstrings cite the paper and figure for the tube construction (L593-610), the sweep (L720-721) and the crest coupling (L753-759); the lateral-area accounting is derived in-line (L656-659). Deductions: the F[w] surrogate coefficients (1.35, 0.85, 0.15, 1.65, 2.2, 1.48) and the 0.85/0.15 wavelength blend are uncited and undocumented as choices (L401-404, L455, L467) (-6); the phase-classifier thresholds (0.011, 0.28, 0.85-2.40, 0.022) cite 'Fig. 2 & Fig. 3' collectively but none individually (L297-317) (-3); the 99th-percentile and 3 q_c low-pass choices in fold_crest_surface_ratio are explained but not justified against the sinusoidal estimate they overshoot (L774-782) (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2016-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d.py L461–L467: 0.85 / 0.15 blend of lambda_c and lambda_fft has no comment or citation <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/654cd6fc/2016-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d.py#L461-L467>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-code-traceability-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-model-fidelity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hannezo, Prost & Joanny (2014) PNAS & Krajnc & Ziherl (2015) PRE 3D epithelial sheet morphology (squamous-to-cuboidal-to-columnar scaling, apico-basal buckling & Gómez-Gálvez scutoid tube packing) — Model fidelity to source: 82/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Law 1 (E_cell, h_0/d_0, d_0, A_0), the L-BFGS-B check of the analytic minimum, the Hessian E''(A_0) = 3 c Gamma_l V_0 / (8 A_0^(5/2)), lambda_c = 2 pi (kappa_eff/K_sub)^(1/4) and the sign-antisymmetric C_0 are implemented as the papers state them (L205-287) and the Pass 3 tube mesh implements the Gómez-Gálvez Voronoi-tube construction faithfully (periodic Delaunay neighbour sets on both surfaces, scutoid = neighbour mismatch, intercalation = edge on exactly one surface, L505-515, L636-643). Deductions: the continuum relaxation F[w] is a Swift-Hohenberg-type surrogate whose coefficients mu = 1.35 (p - 0.85), alpha = 1.65 asym, BETA = 2.2, the 2.2 (K_y/q_c)^2 anisotropy and the 1.48 h_0 sqrt(mu) amplitude scale (L401-404, L408, L455) are not Hannezo/Krajnc equations and are uncited (-6); the 5-regime phase map is a threshold lookup (K_sub <= 0.011, asym >= 0.28, 0.85 <= AR <= 2.40, K_sub <= 0.022; L309-317) rather than a comparison of the energies of the flat, folded and acinar states, so the phase boundaries are inputs, not outputs (-5); the scutoid mesh fixes the seeds and projects them radially - the lateral faces are trapezoid/triangle areas (L656-662), nothing is minimised and the apical/basal tessellations cannot respond to Gamma_l, so the 'energy saving' is a geometric comparison, not an equilibrium (-5); kappa_max is taken as the 99th percentile of a low-passed w_xx (L777-782), a numerical choice that drives s_crest to 3.33 against the 2.30 sinusoidal estimate from the same WT geometry (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2016-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d.py L309–L317: classify_epithelial_phase: hard-coded thresholds decide acinus / folds / flat; phase boundaries are not energy comparisons <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/654cd6fc/2016-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d.py#L309-L317>",
        "2016-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d.py L401–L408: mu_buckling = max(p - 0.85, 0.15) * 1.35, alpha_curv = 1.65 asym, spec_penalty + 2.2 (K_y/q_c)^2 - uncited surrogate coefficients in F[w] <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/654cd6fc/2016-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d.py#L401-L408>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.2e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-morphometric-validation> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hannezo, Prost & Joanny (2014) PNAS & Krajnc & Ziherl (2015) PRE 3D epithelial sheet morphology (squamous-to-cuboidal-to-columnar scaling, apico-basal buckling & Gómez-Gálvez scutoid tube packing) — Morphometric validation: 72/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Twelve measurements with units, references and methods are emitted (L1680-1821), and four of them are real tests of the Pass 3 mechanism against identities that could fail: f_s(1) = 0.0, Euler mean 6.0000 on both surfaces (2508 = 6 x 418), apical-only = basal-only edge counts, lateral-area ratio 0.874 < 1. Deductions: the two headline numbers are circular - aspect-ratio r = 1.0000 (RMSE 0.0041) compares the Law-1 formula with ratios the inputs were fitted to, and the perturbation reference aspect_ratio_ref = 4.4839 is itself c x 5.30 / (4 x 1.10), the formula output (-10); lambda_sim = 0.85 lambda_c + 0.15 lambda_FFT (L467) makes the wavelength r = 0.9993 mostly a test of the analytic formula against K_sub values that were also chosen per tissue, and the RMSE is 11.15 um, not the 1.25 um v2 reported (-5); the specimen references 4.48 and 4.45 are attributed to Hannezo/Štorgel 'tall simple columnar epithelium' without a figure or table pinpoint, and the JSON specimen_histology_reference block stores the script's own output (59.66, 13.31, 4.4833, 264.0, 4.4252) as the reference (-5); the crest-ratio measurement misses its own reference by 44 % (3.326 vs 2.303) and the note attributes it to the sim amplitude 50.4 um / lambda 115.6 um differing from the 42.5 / 136.4 um reference - a disagreement, reported honestly but unresolved (-3); the Spearman rho = 0.977 versus reference 1.0 is a saturation-tie artefact of the sweep grid, not a mechanism test (-2); there is no comparison of the predicted scutoid fraction to any measured scutoid count (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2016-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d.py L461–L467: lambda_sim = 0.85 * lambda_c + 0.15 * lambda_fft: the 'simulated' wavelength is 85 % the analytic prediction <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/654cd6fc/2016-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d.py#L461-L467>",
        "2016-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d.py L924–L934: Pearson r / RMSE / log-log slope of Law-1 predictions vs aspect_ratio_obs - both sides derive from the same JSON row <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/654cd6fc/2016-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d.py#L924-L934>",
        "datasets/epithelial_buckling_3d/epithelial_buckling_3d_reference.json L300–L313: specimen_histology_reference stores mean_layer_height_px 59.66, mean_cell_width_px 13.31, aspect_ratio_h0_d0 4.4833, wavelength_to_height_ratio 4.4252 - the script's own measurements <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/654cd6fc/datasets/epithelial_buckling_3d/epithelial_buckling_3d_reference.json#L300-L313>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-measurement-12-tissue-cross-species-epithelial-aspect-ratio-correlation-mus-musculus-drosophila>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-measurement-apico-basal-spontaneous-curvature-antisymmetry-ratio-c0-basal-c0-apical>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-measurement-buckled-epithelial-fold-acinus-wavelength-correlation-lambda-sim-vs-lambda-obs>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-measurement-cross-species-log-log-aspect-ratio-scaling-exponent-alpha-ar>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-measurement-e-cadherin-knockdown-flattening-control-aspect-ratio-h0-d0>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-measurement-histology-specimen-dimensionless-fold-wavelength-to-thickness-ratio-lambda-c-h0>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-measurement-histology-specimen-empirical-columnar-cell-aspect-ratio-h0-d0-epithelial-sheet-buckling-specimen-jpg>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-measurement-mean-apical-and-basal-neighbour-number-of-the-3d-scutoid-tube-euler-trivalent-torus>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-measurement-scutoid-fraction-of-the-isometric-flat-s-1-3d-tube-mesh>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-measurement-spearman-rank-correlation-of-scutoid-fraction-vs-tube-surface-ratio-s-r-b-r-a>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-measurement-wild-type-fold-crest-surface-ratio-s-crest-1-h0-kappa-max-from-the-relaxed-sheet>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-measurement-wild-type-tall-columnar-intestinal-epithelium-equilibrium-aspect-ratio-h0-d0>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-morphometric-validation-2> ;
    pk1:hasScore 7.2e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-overall> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hannezo, Prost & Joanny (2014) PNAS & Krajnc & Ziherl (2015) PRE 3D epithelial sheet morphology (squamous-to-cuboidal-to-columnar scaling, apico-basal buckling & Gómez-Gálvez scutoid tube packing) — MorphoEval overall 82.4/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The remediation delivers what the script says it delivers: a genuine 3D polyhedral cell mesh on a curved tube (apical and basal periodic Voronoi tessellations of ~418 Hannezo-sized cells, scutoids detected as apical/basal neighbour-set mismatches, intercalations edge-balanced, Euler mean-6 verified on both surfaces, lateral-face area of the scutoid packing 0.87x the frustum packing at the WT crest), swept over surface ratio and coupled to every relaxed tissue through s_crest = 1 + h_0 kappa_max. It honestly labels itself a reduced model (no vertex energy, no T1 dynamics) and two new Lean theorems pin the isometric-limit and Euler identities. Re-scoring against the current code, however, lowers every dimension except where the new work adds: the 12-tissue aspect-ratio r = 1.0000 is circular (tensions back-solved from the observed ratios, no per-row provenance), the 'simulated' wavelength is 85 % the analytic prediction, the WT amplitude equals its reference by rescaling, the reference JSON's specimen block stores the script's own output, the continuum F[w] carries six uncited coefficients, the phase diagram is a threshold lookup with a hard-coded Gamma_b switch, and the fold-crest coupling over-predicts s_crest by 44 % with f_s saturated at ~1.0 for all six buckled/acinar tissues (no discriminating prediction). Overall 82.4 (model impl. 83.3, bio. val. 75.8, repro. 90.3), down from 93.4. Overall 82.4/100 (faithfulness 79.0, reproducibility 90.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 654cd6fc; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 82, Morphological realism / specimen match 78, Parameter expressivity 86, Morphometric validation 72, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 88, Reproducibility package 92. Output judged: docs/media/epithelial_buckling_3d_comparison.png: rendered output of 2016-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d.py at 654cd6fc, image/png, 1143971 B, 2876×1444 px, artifact_sha256 6269de61be241e71465e8aaa782e2860e0546a4d15b07d1fcaf6eceb76858a74 (sha256 6269de61be241e71465e8aaa782e2860e0546a4d15b07d1fcaf6eceb76858a74), spec_fingerprint c058d57a2503a59a583412118501c0ee7c1d08eac1445bb91a576986cd7b311b. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: c058d57a2503a59a583412118501c0ee7c1d08eac1445bb91a576986cd7b311b; artifact_sha256: 6269de61be241e71465e8aaa782e2860e0546a4d15b07d1fcaf6eceb76858a74; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/epithelial_buckling_3d/epithelial_buckling_3d_reference.json=eef9f75ed38ce872..., datasets/epithelial_buckling_3d/epithelial_sheet_buckling_specimen.jpg=cd05cc85a7f49dd2..., datasets/epithelial_buckling_3d/paper_citations.bib=77a77d7dc42170a5..., datasets/epithelial_buckling_3d/scout_manifest.json=99741cb299962b18..., datasets/epithelial_buckling_3d/scutoid_tube_reference.json=85d9db6cbb5b95ff...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-epithelial-buckling-3d-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Hannezo, Prost & Joanny (2014): single-cell energy E_cell(A) = (Gamma_a + Gamma_b) A + c Gamma_l V_0 / (2 sqrt A) gives h_0/d_0 = c Gamma_l / [4 (Gamma_a + Gamma_b)] spanning squamous/cuboidal/columnar; an elastic foundation selects lambda_c = 2 pi (kappa_eff / K_sub)^(1/4); apico-basal tension asymmetry sets a spontaneous curvature whose sign follows Gamma_a - Gamma_b | Krajnc & Ziherl (2015): convexity of the cell energy at equilibrium and the continuum elastic limit of the 3D vertex monolayer | Gómez-Gálvez et al. (2018): on curved tubes the basal/apical surface ratio makes Voronoi tessellations of the two surfaces differ; cells with apico-basal neighbour intercalations (scutoids) appear and their number increases with the surface ratio; reconstructed_in_script: Analytic + L-BFGS-B single-cell equilibrium (L205-271), quartic buckling wavelength (L274-287), a 5-regime threshold phase classifier (L289-317), a 2D pseudo-spectral Swift-Hohenberg-type relaxation F[w] with cubic (spontaneous-curvature) and quartic terms (L323-490), a 12-tissue table and 5 perturbations driven from epithelial_buckling_3d_reference.json (L863-1017), CV segmentation of one CC0 histology micrograph (L1023-1120), and (Pass 3) a doubly periodic Voronoi tube mesh with scutoid detection, surface-ratio sweep and fold-crest curvature coupling (L497-857); transfer_boundary: The 12-tissue Gamma_a/Gamma_b/Gamma_l/K_sub 'norm' values are not measured tensions; they reproduce aspect_ratio_obs through the Law-1 formula to <0.5 % per row and carry no per-row source, so the r = 1.0000 collapse is a parity check of the JSON with itself, not a test against the papers | lambda_sim = 0.85 lambda_c + 0.15 lambda_FFT (L467) and the WT amplitude is rescaled to fold_amplitude_ref_um (L454-455, L999), so the wavelength r = 0.9993 and the WT amplitude 'match' are dominated by construction | The scutoid mesh is a Voronoi projection (seeds fixed, lateral faces evaluated geometrically); it is not a relaxed 3D vertex model and no Gómez-Gálvez figure value is digitised - the scutoid reference values are geometric identities (f_s(1) = 0, mean neighbours 6, Spearman 1) plus a crest ratio derived from the already-pinned WT fold geometry; does_not_claim: A relaxed 3D vertex/scutoid energy (apical, basal and lateral tensions minimised with free vertices), T1 or apico-basal intercalation dynamics, quantitative agreement with the Gómez-Gálvez scutoid counts in salivary gland / egg chamber tubes, measured per-tissue surface tensions, or more than one histological specimen." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2016-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d.py:289-317 and 960-966 — the 5-regime phase diagram is a threshold lookup (K_sub <= 0.011, asym >= 0.28, 0.85 <= AR <= 2.40, K_sub <= 0.022) and the plotting loop injects the acinar asymmetry by switching Gamma_b from 0.75 to 0.40 whenever K_sub <= 0.011. Derive the flat / folded / acinar boundaries by comparing the relaxed energies energy_final of the three seeded states at each grid point (the relaxation already returns them, L395 / L487), and sweep Gamma_a - Gamma_b as a proper axis instead of the K_sub-gated switch.",
        "remediation needed: 2016-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d.py:401-408, 455 and 467 — the continuum F[w] coefficients 1.35, 0.85, 0.15, 1.65, 2.2 (anisotropy), 2.20 (BETA) and 1.48 are uncited. Either derive them from the Hannezo Eqs. (6)-(11) weak-nonlinear expansion (and state the derivation in the docstring) or label them as surrogate fitting constants in the header, the README and the KG yaml so the 'L-BFGS-B relaxed' panels are not read as first-principles predictions.",
        "remediation needed: 2016-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d.py:461-467 and 454-459 — lambda_sim = 0.85 lambda_c + 0.15 lambda_fft and the amplitude rescale to target_amplitude_um make the wavelength correlation (r = 0.9993, RMSE 11.15 um) and the WT amplitude (42.5 = 42.5 um) outputs of the inputs. Report lambda_fft alone as the emergent wavelength (the 64-point grid on a 3 lambda_c box quantises it; use a finer grid or Gaussian peak interpolation), drop the blend, and derive the amplitude from the supercritical balance sqrt(mu/BETA) scaled by h_0 instead of the reference value; then let the comparison fail or pass on its own.",
        "remediation needed: 2016-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d.py:582-662 — the scutoid mesh fixes the seeds and projects them radially; the lateral faces are trapezoid/triangle areas and nothing is minimised, so the mesh cannot respond to Gamma_l, Gamma_a or Gamma_b and the 'lateral area saving' 0.874 is a geometric fact about Voronoi projection, not an equilibrium. Implement the reduced 3D vertex step the Pass 3 header promises as the residual: relax the apical and basal seed positions (or vertex positions) under E = Gamma_a A_a + Gamma_b A_b + Gamma_l A_lat with the volume constraint, and show that the scutoid fraction at fixed s changes with Gamma_l / (Gamma_a + Gamma_b).",
        "remediation needed: 2016-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d.py:752-791 and 1811-1820 — s_crest from the 99th-percentile of the low-passed spectral curvature is 3.326 against the sinusoidal estimate 2.303 computed from the pinned WT fold geometry (44 % over), because the relaxed sheet's amplitude (50.4 um) and wavelength (115.6 um) differ from the reference 42.5 / 136.4 um; with f_s saturated at 1.0 for every buckled tissue the crest coupling has no discriminating power. Compute s_crest from the reference (A, lambda, h_0) triple per tissue as well as from the sheet, extend the sweep grid between s = 1 and 2.5 where f_s is still rising, and add a measurement comparing the predicted scutoid fraction with a published scutoid count (Gómez-Gálvez 2018 Fig. 2/3 salivary gland or egg chamber values, digitised and vendored with a figure pinpoint).",
        "remediation needed: datasets/epithelial_buckling_3d/epithelial_buckling_3d_reference.json:300-313 with 2016-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d.py:1760-1779 — the specimen_histology_reference block stores the script's own segmentation output (59.66 px, 13.31 px, 4.4833, 264.0 px, 4.4252) as the 'reference', while the measurements compare against 4.48 / 4.45 attributed to Hannezo / Štorgel without a locator. Replace the block with independently obtained values (manual annotation of the same micrograph by a second method, or a Štorgel 2016 table value with its table number) and pin the 4.48 / 4.45 references to a figure or table.",
        "remediation needed: datasets/epithelial_buckling_3d/epithelial_buckling_3d_reference.json:56-236 with 2016-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d.py:880-897 and 924-934 — the per-tissue Gamma_a/Gamma_b/Gamma_l 'norm' values reproduce aspect_ratio_obs through Law 1 to <0.5 % on every row and carry no source, so the 12-tissue aspect-ratio r = 1.0000 / RMSE 0.0041 / alpha = 0.994 is a parity check of the JSON with itself. Either (a) replace the tensions with independently reported values (e.g. Sui et al. 2018 laser-ablation recoil ratios for the wing disc; Krajnc/Štorgel columnar estimates) and report the resulting, imperfect, correlation, or (b) relabel the measurement as 'Law-1 parity' with reference_value 1.0 and remove it from the specimen-match evidence; add a per-row `source` field (paper, figure/table) to every tissue and perturbation row." ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.24e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-parameter-expressivity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hannezo, Prost & Joanny (2014) PNAS & Krajnc & Ziherl (2015) PRE 3D epithelial sheet morphology (squamous-to-cuboidal-to-columnar scaling, apico-basal buckling & Gómez-Gálvez scutoid tube packing) — Parameter expressivity: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The morphospace is exercised along several axes with visible, monotone effects: Gamma_l/Gamma_a and K_sub over a 45x45 grid (L950-976), 12 tissue parameter sets, 5 perturbations, the GIF sweep of lateral tension, and (Pass 3) the surface ratio s over 11 values x 3 seeds (f_s: 0 -> 0.18 -> 0.41 -> 0.71 -> 0.88 -> 0.96 -> 1.0; L712-749), tube radius and lumen side (apical vs basal, L616-619), with CLI overrides --gamma-a/-b/-l, --k-sub, --seed, --tube-radius and --surface-ratio (L1924-1940). Deductions: the acinus region of the phase diagram is produced by switching Gamma_b from 0.75 to 0.40 whenever K_sub <= 0.011 (L963), i.e. the asymmetry that creates the acinus is injected by the plotting loop, not swept (-6); above s ~ 2.5 the scutoid fraction saturates at 1.0, and every buckled/acinar tissue lands at s_crest 2.06-3.33, so the curvature coupling produces the same f_s ~ 1.0 for all six (Panel H) - the parameter has no discriminating effect where the script applies it (-5); the jitter (0.28 d_0) and Lloyd count (2) that set the width of the f_s(s) transition are constants, not exposed or swept (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2016-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d.py L842–L857: All 6 buckled/acinar tissues get f_s in [0.957, 1.0] at their crest ratios; the n_buckled_with_scutoids == n_buckled check cannot fail once s_crest > ~2 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/654cd6fc/2016-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d.py#L842-L857>",
        "2016-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d.py L960–L966: Phase-diagram loop sets gb = 0.40 if k_s <= 0.011 else 0.75 - the acinar asymmetry is hard-wired to the K_sub axis <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/654cd6fc/2016-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d.py#L960-L966>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-parameter-expressivity-2> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-repro-package> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hannezo, Prost & Joanny (2014) PNAS & Krajnc & Ziherl (2015) PRE 3D epithelial sheet morphology (squamous-to-cuboidal-to-columnar scaling, apico-basal buckling & Gómez-Gálvez scutoid tube packing) — Reproducibility package: 92/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`--self-test` runs 11 checks in ~16 s (SHA-256 of 5 files, JSON parity, L-BFGS-B vs analytic, perturbation hierarchy, 5-phase coverage, 12-tissue collapse, specimen CV, two-run bitwise determinism, and Pass 3: Law 4 flat = 0 scutoids / curved > 0 / villus s < 1, Law 5 Euler totals on three meshes, monotone sweep, 6/6 buckled with scutoids and 6/6 flat without, crest spectral-vs-sinusoidal within 25 %, mesh determinism, 12-measurement contract; L1824-1917); the default render regenerates PNG, scutoid PNG and GIF in ~26 s with a fixed seed; all data are vendored. Deductions: the 12-tissue acceptance thresholds (r > 0.998, L1859-1860) guard circular metrics and would pass any JSON built the same way (-3); the crest check tolerates a 25 % spectral-vs-sinusoidal gap and the measured gap is 44 % against the pinned reference, so the self-test cannot catch the s_crest disagreement (-2); matplotlib emits a font-cache warning when MPLCONFIGDIR is unset (-1); the repository README section for this script is not updated for the Pass 3 outputs/CLI (outside this slot's write set, noted not penalised further) (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/repro-package" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2016-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d.py L1857–L1860: 12-tissue thresholds r_aspect > 0.998 and r_lambda > 0.995 - guard metrics that are circular by construction <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/654cd6fc/2016-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d.py#L1857-L1860>",
        "2016-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d.py L1896–L1900: Crest check: spectral vs sinusoidal within rel_tol 0.25; the 44 % gap to the pinned 2.303 reference is not tested <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/654cd6fc/2016-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d.py#L1896-L1900>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-repro-package-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-repro-package-2> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.2e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-source-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hannezo, Prost & Joanny (2014) PNAS & Krajnc & Ziherl (2015) PRE 3D epithelial sheet morphology (squamous-to-cuboidal-to-columnar scaling, apico-basal buckling & Gómez-Gálvez scutoid tube packing) — Source and data traceability: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Five primary sources carry DOIs in the module header (L5-28), `paper_citations.bib` (5 entries) and the dataset README; all five dataset files are SHA-256 pinned and verified fail-closed at every run (L146-187, re-pinned after the bib and the new JSON changed); the new `scutoid_tube_reference.json` states explicitly that its values are identities/derivations and that the Gómez-Gálvez DOI was not re-resolved offline. Deductions: the 12 tissue rows and 5 perturbation rows of `epithelial_buckling_3d_reference.json` have no per-row source, figure or table pinpoint - the Gamma_norm, K_sub_norm, pressure_excess_norm, h0_obs_um and lambda_obs_um values cannot be traced to any of the cited papers from this repository (-6); the specimen reference values 4.48 / 4.45 cite 'Hannezo & Štorgel tall simple columnar epithelium' without a locator (-2); the Gómez-Gálvez DOI is carried on the strength of another slot's entry rather than resolved (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/source-traceability" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "datasets/epithelial_buckling_3d/epithelial_buckling_3d_reference.json L223–L236: Tissue row (small intestine) has Gamma_norm, K_sub_norm, pressure_excess_norm, aspect_ratio_obs, h0_obs_um, lambda_obs_um but no source/figure field <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/654cd6fc/datasets/epithelial_buckling_3d/epithelial_buckling_3d_reference.json#L223-L236>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-source-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-source-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-source-traceability-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-specimen-match> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hannezo, Prost & Joanny (2014) PNAS & Krajnc & Ziherl (2015) PRE 3D epithelial sheet morphology (squamous-to-cuboidal-to-columnar scaling, apico-basal buckling & Gómez-Gálvez scutoid tube packing) — Morphological realism / specimen match: 78/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The 8-panel figure is rendered and readable: Panel E overlays the segmented fold centreline and nuclei on the CC0 columnar-epithelium micrograph, Panel G shows the unrolled apical and basal tessellations with scutoids coloured, the standalone scutoid PNG shows the 3D tube, and Panel C's folded topography is a plausible mucosal fold field. Deductions: the 12-tissue 'specimen' comparison (Panel B) is circular - the predicted ratio is the Law-1 formula evaluated on Gamma_norm values that were chosen to give aspect_ratio_obs (every row agrees to <0.5 %, L880-897 against the JSON rows), so the panel compares the JSON with itself (-8); there is one histological specimen and its segmentation has a 32 % CV in h_0 (59.7 +/- 19.2 px) and a 41 % CV in lambda (264 +/- 110 px) from hand-set colour/thickness thresholds (L1040-1060, L1077-1078), so the 4.48 / 4.45 agreements rest on broad distributions (-5); no real tube or scutoid image (Gómez-Gálvez salivary gland / egg chamber) is compared with the mesh - Panel G/H compare the mesh with its own sweep (-5); Panel D's WT amplitude bar equals its reference because the sheet is rescaled to fold_amplitude_ref_um (L454-455, L999) (-4)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2016-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d.py L454–L459: Buckled sheet amplitude rescaled to target_amplitude_um (the reference amplitude for every perturbation, L999) - WT amplitude 42.5 um matches 42.5 um by rescaling <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/654cd6fc/2016-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d.py#L454-L459>",
        "2016-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d.py L880–L897: Per-tissue Gamma_norm from JSON feed Law 1; predicted h0/d0 equals aspect_ratio_obs by construction (no measured tensions) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/654cd6fc/2016-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d.py#L880-L897>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-specimen-match-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-specimen-match-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-specimen-match-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 7.8e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

